        "side": "new",
        "severity": "low",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Search-param-free key accumulates from keyPrefix instead of its own prefix",
        "explanation": "The recursion passes `keyPrefix + '/' + cacheKeyWithoutSearchParams` as the new keyPrefixWithoutSearchParams. That ignores the incoming `keyPrefixWithoutSearchParams` parameter, which is otherwise only returned at the leaf. Any search params encoded in an ancestor's cache key therefore end up in the 'without search params' key. Today only leaf `__PAGE__` segments carry search params, so the two prefixes are identical for ancestors and nothing breaks yet. If an ancestor segment key ever includes search params, the server key would include them too, and the PPR resume key would stop matching the prerendered key again.",
        "suggestion": "Pass `keyPrefixWithoutSearchParams + '/' + cacheKeyWithoutSearchParams` as the fourth argument.",
        "evidence": "      keyPrefix + '/' + cacheKeyWithoutSearchParams",
        "confidence": 0.7,
        "id": "aa20dd02a03b",
