        "side": "new",
        "severity": "low",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Search-param-free key built from prefix that still has search params",
        "explanation": "The without-search-params key is built from keyPrefix (which includes search params of ancestor segments) rather than keyPrefixWithoutSearchParams. If any non-leaf ancestor segment carries search params, the result won't be truly search-param-free. Usually only the page segment has them, so impact is limited.",
        "suggestion": "Use keyPrefixWithoutSearchParams + '/' + cacheKeyWithoutSearchParams.",
